=== environment ============================================
device        Tesla V100-SXM2-32GB (sm_70), 80 SMs, 96 KiB smem/SM
denominators  peak_gb_s=634.2  peak_tflops=15.603  (MEASURED, not spec)
ridge point   24.6 FLOP/byte -- below this a kernel is memory-bound
              spec-formula bandwidth for reference: 898.0 GB/s
build         MCKE_WITH_CUDA=1
============================================================

shape         8192 x 4096   compulsory bytes 268435456 (256.0 MiB)
algorithmic   three_pass 4N*4 = 512.0 MiB   online 3N*4 = 384.0 MiB
L2 note       each row is 16 KiB; ~160 resident blocks give a ~2.5 MiB
              working set, which FITS the T4's 4 MiB L2 -- so three_pass's
              2nd and 3rd reads may never reach DRAM. If it beats its own
              traffic model, that is the finding, not an error.

