=== three-pass vs online (RESULTS.md section 3c) ===========
  three_pass 0.820 ms (327.3 GB/s)   online 0.585 ms (459.1 GB/s)   1.40x
  PREDICTION 4/3 = 1.33x from traffic alone (3 reads -> 2), less any L2
  reuse, so realistically 1.0-1.25x. NOT 3x -- "one pass" names the
  statistics passes, not the memory passes.
  Neither reaches 100% of 634.2 GB/s BY CONSTRUCTION: the denominator is
  compulsory traffic (2N*4), and the extra passes are exactly the gap.

=== numerics ==============================================
  max |sum(row) - 1|   three_pass 1.701e-07   online 2.184e-07   (ratio 1.28x)
  PREDICTION: online is 2-5x LESS accurate, and that is expected, not a
  defect. Three-pass computes numerator and denominator from the identical
  expression with the same m, so they are bit-consistent; online builds the
  denominator through a chain of rescaled partials and then computes a fresh
  numerator, so they agree only to within accumulated rounding.

